      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, and we only expose addNetworkPolicyListener() and removeNetworkPolicyListener() in this CL.\nIf we wnat to remove @SuppressLint, we can rename this class to NetworkPolicyCallback and the codes might look like\n\n1. maybe rename NetworkPolicyListenerProxy to NetworkPolicyCallbackProxy\n\n2. rename methods [add|remove]NetworkPolicyListener() to [register|unregister]NetworkPolicyCallback()\n\n   registerNetworkPolicyCallback(NetworkPolicyCallback cb) {\n       ...\n       registerListener(cb)   // here\u0027s the original method to register a listener\n   }\n\n   unregisterNetworkPolicyCallback(NetworkPolicyCallback) {\n        ...\n        unregisterListener(cb.getCallback())   //rename from getListener() in NetworkPolicyListener\n   }\n\nSo, only inconsistent naming inside the two new APIs.\n\n\nIf we don\u0027t want to expose @SystemApi with the annotation @SuppressLint. I can upload a new patchset to rename it as long as we can accept the inconsistencies I mentioned above.",
