      "writtenOn": "2020-01-14T10:23:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This parameter needs to be explained. I think it\u0027s a bitmap of NetworkPolicyManager RULE_* constants. If so, then the documentation needs to say that it is. And the constants need to be @SystemApi and you need an IntDef for them. Looking at existing examples, I think you need something like:\n\n    /**\n     * No specific rule set.\n     * @hide\n     */\n    @SystemApi\n    public static final int RULE_NONE \u003d 0;\n\n    /**\n     * Allow traffic on metered networks.\n     * @hide\n     */\n    @SystemApi\n    public static final int RULE_ALLOW_METERED \u003d 1 \u003c\u003c 0;\n\n... other RULE_* constants follow, all @SystemApi ...\n\n    /**\n     * Per-UID network traffic rules.\n     *\n     * @hide\n     */\n    @SystemApi\n    @IntDef(flag \u003d true, prefix \u003d {\"RULE_\"}, value \u003d {\n            RULE_NONE,\n            RULE_ALLOW_METERED,\n            ...\n    })\n    @Retention(RetentionPolicy.SOURCE)\n    public @interface Rule {}\n\n... then, later on, annotate the parameters:\n\n    public void onUidRulesChanged(int uid, @Rule int uidRules) {",
